Feature: promotion admits a draft the ticket itself converts, and QA refuses one that never was

  BL-626 closed a real hole: a ticket promoted against an acceptance pointer
  that resolved to nothing was worked and closed with its contract never once
  executed. It closed it at PROMOTION, by refusing every `.feature.draft`
  pointer outright.

  That refusal cannot tell two different tickets apart. A PARKED draft belongs
  to a slice somebody else builds later - refusing it is right, because nothing
  in that ticket will ever materialise it. A SELF-CONVERTING draft belongs to
  the very slice chartered to rename it, register its step handler, and repoint
  `acceptance:` in the same parcel - the shape `specifier.prompt` has mandated
  since 2026-08-30, and the only shape available when committing a live
  `.feature` ahead of its handler would throw the runner for every other parcel
  (BL-233).

  Refusing the second kind is a deadlock no role can clear: the ticket cannot
  promote until the draft is converted, and the draft cannot be converted until
  the ticket promotes. Twelve live tickets sit in it, two of them `high`
  expedited defects at the head of the Article 3.2.4 lane.

  The gate moves rather than disappears. Promotion admits a draft the ticket
  pins itself to converting; the documenter->QA edge refuses one that arrives
  still a draft. Allowed in, forbidden out - so BL-626's silence stays closed
  at the end where a contract can actually have gone unexecuted.

  Background:
    Given a ticket eligible for promotion into the active backlog

  # BL-1340 self-converting-draft-01
  Scenario: a draft the ticket pins itself to converting is promoted
    Given the candidate's acceptance names its own draft
    And the candidate pins that draft's conversion in its own charter
    When the coordinator promotes the next eligible ticket
    Then the candidate is promoted

  # BL-1340 self-converting-draft-02
  Scenario: a parked draft the ticket does not convert is still refused
    Given the candidate's acceptance names its own draft
    And the candidate pins no conversion of that draft
    When the coordinator promotes the next eligible ticket
    Then the promotion is refused
    And the refusal names the draft as parked with no conversion pinned

  # BL-1340 self-converting-draft-03
  Scenario: buildability never reorders the expedite lane
    Given an expedited defect whose acceptance names a self-converting draft
    And a non-expedited candidate whose acceptance names an existing feature
    When the coordinator promotes the next eligible ticket
    Then the expedited defect is promoted first

  # BL-1340 self-converting-draft-04
  Scenario: a parcel still naming a draft cannot reach QA
    Given a parcel whose ticket acceptance still names a draft
    When the documenter sends it to QA
    Then the handoff is refused
    And the refusal names the unconverted draft
